[I] Internet Object Cache

[T] Squid is a fully-featured HTTP/1.0 proxy which is almost HTTP/1.1
[T] compliant. Squid offers a rich access control, authorization and logging
[T] environment to develop web proxy and content serving applications.

[U] https://www.squid-cache.org/

[A] Duane Wessels
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/server
[F] JAIL CROSS

[E] opt cyrus-sasl2

[L] GPL
[V] 7.7

[D] 287ec5c5aa9be063032cda85cf851d2177ba2763931764f0b8535aa9 squid-7.7.tar.xz https://github.com/squid-cache/squid/releases/download/SQUID_7_7/

[ $prefix_auto = 1 ] && prefix=opt/squid && set_confopt

var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' "-I$root$(pkgprefix includedir openldap) -L$root$(pkgprefix libdir openldap)"

var_append confopt ' ' --enable-follow-x-forwarded-for
